A||||3||Formula||3.4 crate motor swap, starter problems.||||1||
Z||000000||Formula||11-11-2001||04:14 PM||||Has anyone had any problems with the starters on their 3.4s.  Mine keeps grinding and then completly missing the flexplate.  I put a lot of different spacers, shims, etc in it to get it to work but nothing is helping.<P>I hope its not the flexplate, if it is I'm putting a standard in it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||11-11-2001||04:19 PM||||What did you use to make the starter holes in the block?  That would help verify that, if you did it right.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||11-11-2001||04:28 PM||||I'm thinking that the template holes were not drilled in the correct place for the mounting of the starter on the 3.4 block.  The other potential is the toothed gear that meshes with the flex plate is not the correct one.  Mismatched gears.<P>If it is missing the flexplate, theholes may not have been drilled deep enough, so the starter doesnot line up.<P>The only thing Bob Steiger told me with the starter alignment on my 3.4 was to be careful with the alignment.  Driving the mounting bolts in too deep can crack the block at the starter mount position, if the holes were not drilled deep enough initially.  Alignment was done with shims on the mounting bolts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||11-11-2001||11:55 PM||||I used the drilling kit that I got off the forum that a lot of other people have used.  The holes were drilled all the way through the block I believe.   So it might be the flexplate mesh, would I be able to use a different starter that would work with that mesh?||||reg||1
